# Frontend development

## Prefer existing structure

- Shell: `DepartmentLayout` / `DepartmentLayoutImpl`; domain shells (QMS, DocumentControl, Roster) where already used.
- Do not introduce a new layout framework; do not revive unused `AppShell` / `AppShellV2` without an explicit consolidation plan.
- Primitives: `frontend/src/components/shared/*`, `components/UI/*`, brand/liquid-glass kits already in tree.
- Styling: `styles/tokens.css` + `styles/index.css` import order. No competing token systems or Tailwind introduction.
- Data: `services/apiClient.ts` + domain `services/*` + TanStack Query. No second HTTP stack.

## Routing

- Respect dispatcher → `PortalRouteSurface` → `portalRoutes` ownership.
- Do not duplicate routes/pages/services for the same workflow. One live owner per URL/experience.
- Path builders / manifests: prefer `app/canonicalRoutes.ts`, `portalRouteManifest.ts`, QMS registries.

## UX completeness

- Complex workspaces may use tabs and vertical drawers when that matches existing patterns.
- Every visible action must work or be clearly unavailable (disabled + reason). No placeholder “complete” UI.
- Verify responsive behavior at representative desktop, wide-desktop, tablet, and mobile widths.
- Operational grids/workspaces must use available viewport space effectively and must not introduce unexplained dead space, clipping, or unnecessary horizontal scrolling.
- After implementation: check browser console and network (failed requests, auth errors).

## When unsure

Search for an existing page/service/shell before adding files. If two implementations exist, extend the canonical owner documented in-repo (especially QMS guardrails).
